      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T18:32:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That can\u0027t work. db845 needs to use the same GKI image as everyone else so if it is built into GKI it can\u0027t be a module for db845c. So one of these options must be taken:\n\n1. Don\u0027t specify MULTICOLOR in gki_defconfig at all (it\u0027s a vendor module enabled in device specific fragments as db845c does)\n\n2. Build MULTICOLOR into gki_defconfig as \u003dy. Remove it from db845c\n\n3. Build as GKI module by adding to gki_defconfig as \u003dm. Remove from db845c.\n\nSo 2 questions:\nIs this needed for all android devices? (option 2 and 3)\nIf so, does it need to be built-in (option 2)",
      "parentUuid": "d1cf5321_cde819dc",
      "revId": "04019cb610c69086e74568fed3112147360d1824",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
